data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":754,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_015e8db9ee4f072a016acb52df0264819589928e18f3a02421","object":"response","created_at":1791709919,"completed_at":1791709934,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_015e8db9ee4f072a016acb52e0340481958079ea162ebc952e","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Considering textarea implementation**\n\nI need to ensure that the textarea leading newline in HTML is correctly handled since the parser strips the initial LF. It seems I must always prefix with a newline to maintain proper formatting. Also, since the browser converts CR to LF, I'll have to handle this during storage with the exact API. I might need to implement the LF prefix and conduct tests for migration, possibly using the old schema for inspection."}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqy1Lj7w6BzOL8IaMldTQrtyyFfVrVvUAuVtip3jwOgCf2N53IopDR3pCXGSr3bzCLcjTW2IfqzQ9zuBwEqb324AN3r8BdfDGiv3xWxiypDF46hp1nLw9by46R97qMQLauiJbfbItDXpCJ5Q5O3y2_H6EF8FPdMTxP0v2WrlA9SHSHRKDQ75SbTkTTJlJioS4KyixXlth1QDYYiiyVn9nFAjQMTD_gstUHg9C40OPjJBtwegglZI7LjGCl4l0WfJRHSkIwMxQEibDV35VH16SQTWxKV0GFk1wv7kDCcmdiSyU7NnhblR8uvd9XTegajsrXbovbkX3FDJKO2mO_PFn7HSnaulG7R4qeas3dhnJFFjkMoSRPuIHbjVqisL2knJ6nr3dajtjeN1KQe3riD7YVA-yddip_oKoeyxvGtQCGsHPSNbDdIbjUo9nCxo6foufpJeKhc2Yw7eWR6hnZzq7oNHpMb9h0sttY0_iiRBYqiDVchZMgt-9oneHY7Q0TGnFDO6T9B4sukiGAU7K8k0Wof8dXXtHIwUIfHJSEpLg4jJXxg1gEDdepn5Zv61LPYN8OKbEczRR9ifkqmfy2kXjvLNOTq_A04yKhKknL-hlXKqv89GSSiZfsAVpyKVR03pDjtp5U_1M-ob4IrQClzsKywrKM1sE-pfCHYxVo_gZrrcZf6pEihoNaw9XmjQm27Ffw1JycpExKxeyQMbNRvfOxg3yJMvHhfUYAcNQ3UfPuFjvaxGgplsfh_ZW-oLk4XDkQdJYxq4SFmfv0PW7I6NyvVHVw8LDTbjw8bldcCIDPni7_7OIclur2CEJ44Li73YO5UrlMvgRzxttOG0nbIh5L1nGkVgrhMC5Dp-ZFn0QnV8VU2BDank9s9oy_Z7oHRSKqV0vAXTojyATq8yJPDU01lL-oFzNuIUz4944gtgzOf4f7JJwS7v_mKwq9yjvHYJXeMARgxjHReSx8-w5ou1kWuwudUDsgGzJku2opvP4VKCM7PPGHaw76xcaMYOZ9zUN2Fmook8IvLbhs1zMyfz7mdaHBsZRu5M9uuWWM4i7mBnVZbsYrqiKR4meG2J4cHaCspZK_AnRCa4fP9hizy9umMjHufw3X793S1LgPYtTaVUB2UUuRP67DPr_kr8Opo6GWUWqe3CQx5aijoTyI23dhxTUmGYF2cU2pz9-fLd3O84XYoG7jOskjIXgK5Ym3N8nsaCRTKKroUP2rlQ48xV7AzsRgU0pGEqEwK7mg0uWg0WceGi5vM5ajtIJx2OhhbRoOd1xJNcVPhyMkPfyVgx3GO26e0W_g81KccrDG-aOFZX6LrEo6ECV8fxhQ5Y1w7xUd5Y33DIsbAMEMLjONjo9_nZfjGawp8Vu70TgMXSnsXGZxawn2-XEZpmsnWfVXQ-iLV4kp9PYYGceGfNedvOvAX9MSeibMa3DnZvV23UlI7Rb8_UQTUWtCAHACBUacuiqvgIt6hVmAdGh8JPPrM4sLRtc9t1-XFO-LRVEtT9CWa-zqJyJgrUMsOHYH8NGDGCgk-Mj4w34_2SnC-VXDeZt0YfHLc8JIveVpdY8fJdz6rgYy1Dp3_u7-zqohUlZZKV3TTVcp2vsfR38oqehJyQ7W0xz00AM7ikCIBfygskWTC2IRGOVdKmWFTS5WPoRWYfc0IKjoUs3Lrm-gRNxIVO1oW74rYwijOktCZpwfBhVNavMp8bghQD3_BrdHJqEJ16NUo1Lpjk6qBmQnUhtItUL_C0Qi-54N8p_fIxhqxqZ_C5QFRPE6iLqOSgIt55dZIdSYemgX_D01lK3kZ4RxtepImF9XU4YKMcrwNQLI-WAlZAI597Kllc1rUjpHuMXXfxOrNUszD8A9_7OlpjERLcuLlV0GdrDH4aYiBmx4LtbB3PNbCzpROvhm_-9Q0WJ8Okjtmp4melFWbrTv_28LcjIcT7VAtHFqS